>I'm curious: is the same thing true of foocubi encounters? I've heard of 
>people talking about using them to level up, without any apparent worry that 
>they may actually level down. 

Yes, but the situation is rather different. Firstly, good stats reduce the
odds of a bad *cubus effect; the "new man" effect is always equally likely
to be harmful or helpful.

Secondly, a bad *cubus encounter puts you 1 XP below the number needed for
your old level, just like a vampire attack. If you are already past the
point at which you have a serious chance of gaining levels by killing
things, no harm has been done provided you can swat a popcorn monster
before suffering the _same_ adverse effect again. Even in that case
one-half the lost levels can be regained from full healing.

Conversely, a bad "new man" effect puts you at a random amount of
experience consistent with the new level, and reduces your recorded
maximum level so full healing will not be effective.
